  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Inclusive Safety: Supporting Jamaica Strategy for Citizen Security, School Safety and Gender Based Violence Reduction</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action supports the Government of Jamaica&apos;s efforts to create a safer, more inclusive society, addressing the root causes of violence and promoting gender equality. It aims to contribute to safer communities, reduce crime and violence, in particular gender based violence, and improve the overall security landscape in Jamaica by fostering coordination among various stakeholders, improving governance and capacity, and providing targeted interventions for vulnerable populations.Activities focus on strengthening coordination at policy and operational levels, improving data systems, promoting community engagement, enhancing school safety, renovating community spaces, and supporting survivors of GBV. Other activities include academic improvement initiatives, case management for at-risk youth, and maintaining policy dialogue with stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
